body:
@NeoTech: re-check request. Your 03:53Z request (merge current main, keep both sides with #546, re-run the sinker suites, solid_law_goldens and clippy) is done at `cbfbf6c6`.

The merge surfaced a real interaction: main's `burn_compensated` ignored this PR's undersize stand-off, so a plain merge would burn a rough pass into the finish allowance. The fix (decision recorded, yours to overrule) makes the wear maths read the stand-off and compensate only the depth actually burned, matching `worn_tip`, so the planned burn is the burn the sim checks. With no stand-off set, the burn is byte-identical to main. Reverting the fix makes `sinker_undersize::a_rough_finish_pair_reaches_the_finished_size_in_the_sim` fail.

The other session's safety review at this head is clean: the formula is derived independently, and 6 mutations go red. `needs-rework` is yours to clear.
